      description: "Nalmefene is a longer-acting opioid-receptor antagonist that competitively blocks and displaces opioids from opioid receptors, restoring respiratory drive and reducing central nervous system depression; in the United States, it is supplied as Opvee 2.7 mg/0.1 mL single-use nasal spray and Zurnai 1.5 mg/0.5 mL single-use intramuscular or subcutaneous auto-injector. It is not naloxone, naltrexone, or the naloxone component of buprenorphine/naloxone. Its longer pharmacologic effect may reduce some recurrence risk, but emergency services and ventilation remain mandatory because exposure may be massive, mixed, delayed, or caused by a partial agonist. Both rescue products are prescription products for patients 12 years and older under their current labels.",
