      administrationTiming: ["Give immediately for suspected opioid respiratory depression while activating 911 and providing ventilation or CPR; diagnostic certainty is not required before lifesaving support.", "Opvee is one 2.7 mg/0.1 mL spray in one nostril; Zurnai delivers 1.5 mg/0.5 mL intramuscularly or subcutaneously into the anterolateral thigh, through clothing if necessary, and is held in place for the labeled 3 seconds.", "If the patient does not respond or relapses, use a new device every 2 to 5 minutes according to the exact label while emergency care continues."],
