      keyLabs: ["Do not delay nalmefene or ventilation for a toxicology result because overdose reversal is a clinical emergency and prolonged hypoventilation causes hypoxic injury.", "Trend respiratory rate, chest movement, pulse oximetry, and capnography when available, and obtain a blood gas when ventilation remains impaired because apparent awakening or an acceptable oxygen saturation does not prove adequate carbon-dioxide clearance.", "Check glucose and use ECG, electrolytes, renal and hepatic tests, toxicology studies, and complication-directed imaging as indicated because co-ingestants, organ failure, aspiration, trauma, or stroke can explain persistent coma and alter monitoring needs."],
